[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 518,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 497,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73168,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 497,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intravascular large B-cell lymphoma is a distinctive type of aggressive B-cell lymphoma characterized by exclusively intravascular growth.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 519,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 498,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73169,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 498,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9712/3 Intravascular large B-cell lymphoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 520,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 499,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73170,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 499,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2A81.1 Intravascular large B-cell lymphoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 521,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 500,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73171,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 500,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> angiotropic large cell lymphoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 522,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 501,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73172,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 501,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 523,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 502,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73173,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 502,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The brain is nearly always involved; spinal cord involvement is less common.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 524,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 503,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73174,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 503,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Except for the solely cutaneous cases, CNS involvement occurs in 75&ndash;85% of cases {11890850}. The hallmark intravascular growth leads to clinical symptoms mimicking those of cerebral infarction or subacute encephalopathy {24931821}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 525,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 504,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73175,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 504,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intravascular large B-cell lymphoma is rare and usually manifests in adults. The median patient age is 70&nbsp;years (range: 34&ndash;90&nbsp;years). There is no sex predilection {30111607}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 526,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 505,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73176,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 505,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 527,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 506,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73177,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 506,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Absence of CD29 and CD54 (ICAM1) expression is thought to underlie the tumour cells&rsquo; inability to migrate transvascularly {10685637}. Expression levels of the chemokine receptors CXCR5, CCR6, and CCR7 are decreased, and MMP2 and MMP9 are not expressed. Thus, the tumour cells express molecules that enable their adhesion to the endothelium but not those involved in extravasation {30111607}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 534,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 513,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73178,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 513,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Macroscopy reveals infarcts (acute and/or old), necrosis, and/or haemorrhage, although abnormalities may be inconspicuous.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 528,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 507,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73179,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 507,
        "headingText": "<p>Microscopically, large atypical B cells are present, confined to the lumina of cerebral blood vessels; they may occlude these vessels, but they do not invade into the brain parenchyma, although, exceptionally, a few cells may extravasate. Immunohistochemically, the neoplastic B cells typically show a strong expression of CD20. However, exceptional CD20-negative cases have been reported that require immunostaining for additional B-cell markers (e.g. CD79a and PAX5) {30111607}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-10-26T15:29:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 529,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 508,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73180,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 508,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 530,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 509,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73181,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 509,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Detection of clonal rearrangement of the IG genes may be helpful for the diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 533,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 512,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73182,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 512,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/45/167/22807\" target=\"_blank\">#22807</a>Box&nbsp;10.04 .</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 531,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 510,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73183,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 510,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Staging should determine involvement of other organs because intravascular lymphoma may be widely disseminated.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 532,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 511,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73184,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 511,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis of intravascular large B-cell lymphoma involving the CNS is poor. Methotrexate-based chemotherapy is beneficial in a subset of patients {23217063}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:12:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]